      </entryLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Daemon of Slaanesh" id="1d23-eda4-7525-eedf" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="50b1-96f5-fbda-1c64" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Daemon of Slaanesh" id="f9c0-85c3-0153-7f20" hidden="false">
              <description>Daemons of Slaanesh have the Daemon, Fleet, Hatred (Daemon of Khorne) and Rending special rules. In addition, units composed entirely of Daemons of Slaanesh Run an additional 3&quot;. Units that are entirely composed of Cavalry models instead Run an additional 6&quot;. Vehicles that are not Walkers move an extra 3&quot; whenever they move Flat Out instead.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Bulbous Ooze" id="37c8-6a50-cbac-1b6d" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="65"/>
      </costs>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Bulbous Ooze" id="ad6d-3627-7b6b-4b4f" hidden="false" typeId="35bb-3fdd-dd9d-1fc8" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="2ba2-3a82-dfb7-7849">Fortification</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="M" typeId="e8fa-a6b3-0e8c-18aa">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="9660-0df5-9c5d-3604">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="565d-bf36-9e7e-29b5">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="23ae-6026-aebd-abc3">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="f6db-a6a5-71d2-71c5">6</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="a763-cbc8-2080-a4fb">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="ea41-893b-3f82-5482">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="d535-b745-b613-a7ab">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="3b5e-ab67-ed36-a88f">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Save" typeId="d33e-1fdc-0c00-8cb8">5+</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="3df9-f556-8725-fe75"/>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Rot of Nurgle" id="5423-c8a1-9a87-6a97" hidden="false">
          <description>At the start of the game, place the Bulbous Ooze anywhere on the gameboard, at least 18&quot; away from any enemy models, and outside of the enemy deployment zone.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Pus Explosion" id="9193-c02f-1e21-9c8d" hidden="false">
          <description>If at any point, a unit that does not contain the Daemon of Nurgle special rule ends it&apos;s movement phase within 3&quot; of a bulbous ooze, or the bulbous ooze  is otherwise destroyed then at the end of that player&apos;s turn, the bulbous ooze immediatly explodes and the controlling player rolls on the table below. 

2D6
1-2: The bulbous ooze shrivles up, nothing happens and the ooze is removed from play. 
3-6: The ooze explodes, coating itself on anything nearby. Any model within 6&quot; suffers a Str5 AP- attack with the Poisoned (4+) special rule. The Bublous Ooze is removed from play.
7-10: Nesting Nurglings within the Ooze awaken. Immediatly place a single unit of nurglings anywhere within 6&quot; of the Bulbous Ooze. Any model within 6&quot; suffers a Str5 AP- attack with the Poisoned (4+) special rule. The Bublous Ooze is removed from play.
11-12: The bulbous ooze explodes and with the blessings of nurgle, grows anew. Roll 6D6. On any roll of a 5+, a new bulbous ooze may be created within 12&quot; of the original model so long as it is further than 3&quot; from any enemy models. This bulbous ooze may not then create further bulbous oozes, but otherwise plays as normal. Nesting Nurglings within the Ooze awaken. Immediatly place a single unit of nurglings anywhere within 6&quot; of the Bulbous Ooze. Any model within 6&quot; suffers a Str5 AP- attack with the Poisoned (4+) special rule. The Bublous Ooze is removed from play. The original Bulbous Ooze is removed from play.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Daemonic Formations" id="ef40-6a4c-4383-87e1" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="8b0a-52ee-6aed-3172" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Nurgle Formations" id="5025-5606-03f1-dbde" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="d6c0-1ba5-0968-89a6" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Rotswarm" id="ce73-2a7d-4e37-ddbb" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="ecd5-adfb-ebba-a631" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Corrosive Slime" id="9957-7aa7-d0ab-4e24" hidden="false">
                  <description>All units in a Rotswarm have the Hammer of Wrath (1) special rule and these attacks have the Poisoned (4+) special rule.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Dubious Command" id="5e7e-e471-6157-fdab" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Warlord of a Rotswarm Detachment must be a Herald of Nurgle. In addition, you may not take any allied detachments as a part of this force.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule name="Harbinger of Nurgle" id="191d-a86c-5bf2-9f8c" hidden="false">
                  <description>If the Herald of Nurgle from this formation is a Lesser Locus of Virulence, Greater Locus of Fecundity or an Exalted Locus of Contagion, the special rules associated with that locus affect all units from this Formation that are within 12&quot; of him. If such a unit is also affected by another locus, they will receieve both benefits.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Nauseous Contagion" id="d752-83bc-2887-17e0" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="e918-6b5e-3d85-947a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
              </costs>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Nauseous Contagion" id="b2cc-3af4-f38c-e9ef" hidden="false">
                  <description>The Nauseous Contagion, a vile assembly within the Pestilent Host of Nurgle, emerges as a noxious harbinger of decay and despair. Comprised of Plague Drones, Plaguebearers, and the lumbering, daemon-infested Great Unclean One, this formation blankets the battlefield in a grotesque miasma of buzzing flies and putrid odors. 

Effects
• At the start of each Assault phase, enemy units that are locked in combat with any units part of a Nausous Contagion must pass a Leadership Test or reduce their Toughness characteristics by 1 for the duration of that phase. 
• Enemy units cannot fire Overwatch or Return Fire against units that are a part of a Nauseous Contagion. 

Limitations
• Any allied units which do not have the Mark of Nurgle or are not a Daemon of Nurgle may not stand within 6&quot; of a model that is a part of a Nauseous Contagion formation. Friendly Models that arrive via Deepstrike or must cross within 6&quot; of a unit that is apart of a Nausous Contagion must immedialy move out of the 6&quot; radius and take a Difficult Terrain test. Units that have deepstriked in this fashion must make a test as if they had landed inside Difficult Terrain. 
• A Nauseous Contagion must contain at least one Great Unclean One, and this model must be the Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
    </selectionEntry>
